* Frozen netlist snapshot for record 20260921-021359-2422cac
* source     : sim/sar-logic-timing-gates-xl/testbench/tb_sar_logic_timing_gates_xl.spice
* sha256     : 8236a343dfff18984e2b6c0a3c4b14e6caefb24f267d519156b54fbba13c63fa
* This is a verbatim copy taken at record time. Do not edit.
* ==================================================================
* tb_sar_logic_timing -- what the synchronous choice actually buys,
* measured rather than asserted (issue #11, DR-0008).
*
* GENERATED by design/sar-logic/flow/gen_sar_ctrl_gates_tb.py -- do not edit.
*
* ISSUE #311: this deck instantiates ONE loop of the five-loop
* family above (ok/lt/xl/bad/tie), not all five. ngspice advances
* one GLOBAL timestep for a whole deck, so five clock-sharing
* sar_ctrl_a instances sharing one file force each other's step
* down to the union of their switching activity -- measured at up
* to ~100x the cost per simulated ns of running one loop alone
* (sim/sar-logic-timing-gates/investigations/
* 20260917-issue-303-five-loop-composition-cost.md). The loops
* are electrically independent -- each has its own sar_ctrl_a
* instance, CDAC/comparator and stimulus, sharing only the `clk`
* stimulus and the `vdd_gate` supply -- so splitting them changes
* NOTHING about what is measured, only how many loops share one
* deck. The measurement definitions, bounds and 8.5 us duration
* are UNCHANGED from the five-loop composition.
*
* `xl`: 50 ns delay -- 80% of the bit cycle consumed,
* still correct. Not the survey's original guess: an
* earlier draft of the five-loop deck used 55 ns and
* measured a real failure (max|err| = 2 LSB against a
* >= 1 LSB threshold). Bisecting against the same
* behavioural DAC/comparator model found the true
* boundary between 50 ns (exact) and 52 ns (max|err| =
* 1 LSB, already over the 0.5 LSB bound). 50 ns is kept
* as the bracket point precisely because it is the
* largest round number this model measures as exact,
* not because it was the original guess -- CLAUDE.md
* requires a measured number here, not an assumed one.
* DR-0010 records the gap between the survey's slack
* estimate and this measured boundary; the shortfall is
* attributed to this testbench's RC DAC-settling model
* (tau = 2.56 ns) consuming part of the delay budget the
* survey treated as separate, not to a synchronous-logic
* problem.
*
* ==================================================================

.param vref={vdd_val}
